# Line endings: normalised in the repository, native in the worktree.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Without it, what lands in a commit depends on
# whoever's `core.autocrlf` happens to run, and any file written by
# tooling that does not convert arrives as LF into an otherwise CRLF
# worktree. The cost is not theoretical: staging this repo on 9 October
# 2026 produced a 1,048-line diff on `src/lib/subscription.ts` of which
# 372 lines were real changes. Roughly 60% of that commit was
# line-ending churn — which buries real edits in review and makes
# `git blame` useless on the files it touches.
#
# `text=auto` stores text as LF and checks it out as the platform
# prefers. Git sniffs binary content and leaves it untouched.
* text=auto

# Explicit for the extensions worth never guessing about.
*.ts    text
*.tsx   text
*.js    text
*.mjs   text
*.cjs   text
*.json  text
*.css   text
*.md    text
*.html  text
*.txt   text
*.yaml  text
*.yml   text
*.rules text

# Never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.webm  binary
*.mp4   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
